          "text": "Higher maternal BMI",
          "is_correct": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "ANSWER: C Anorexia nervosa is independently predicted by female sex, infant feeding problems, maternal depressive symptoms, and a history of undereating. High self-esteem and higher maternal BMI are protective.",
