          "text": "This diagnosis is not attributable to a concurrent medical condition.",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "correct_answer": {
        "letter": "C",
        "option_id": "85f158f1-99fa-4743-a678-cffdba5f4e5a",
        "text": "This diagnosis is related to the way body weight or shape is experienced by the patient."
      },
      "correct_answers": [
        {
          "letter": "C",
          "option_id": "85f158f1-99fa-4743-a678-cffdba5f4e5a",
          "text": "This diagnosis is related to the way body weight or shape is experienced by the patient.",
          "is_correct": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "ANSWER: C Avoidant/restrictive food intake disorder involves an eating/feeding disturbance that is not due to unavailability of food, observation of cultural norms, anorexia nervosa, bulimia nervosa, or a medical condition. Evidence of a disturbance in experience of body shape or weight excludes this diagnosis.",
